      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now KFENCE is compiled into GKI kernels, but disabled at runtime, because CONFIG_KFENCE_SAMPLE_INTERVAL is set to 0.\nThis does not add any extra overhead to the kernels yet (no memory allocated, no runtime penalty), except for a few Kb of extra code (when I looked, there was no increase in code size - probably we got lucky to fill some existing gaps).\n\nAs for performance, Binder benchmarks show nearly zero slowdown:\n - between 0.5% speedup and 1% slowdown for the sampling value of 500ms (the recommended one);\n - between 1% and 0% speedup for the sampling value of 1000ms (which pretty much characterizes the noise level).",
